        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Local scope",
            "id": 86990,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Variables created inside a function have a <strong>local scope</strong>, like <code>bonus</code> here.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"add_bonus\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(salary)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" bonus = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" print(salary + bonus)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"add_bonus(\" /><text value=\"1900\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"24\" endIndex=\"29\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;bonus&quot;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"2000\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>bonus</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Variables created inside a function have a <strong>local scope</strong>. Give the local <code>bonus</code> the value <code>100</code> so the code prints <code>2000</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"add_bonus\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(salary)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" bonus = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" print(salary + bonus)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"add_bonus(\" /><text value=\"1900\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"24\" endIndex=\"29\" /><option startIndex=\"32\" endIndex=\"35\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"salary\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;100&quot;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"2000\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>bonus</code>, followed by <code>100</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Local scope 2",
            "id": 86991,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>With a local scope, we can only access or update the variable within the function that created it. Try setting <code>bonus</code> to <code>200</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"add_bonus\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(salary)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" bonus = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" bonus = \" /><text value=\"200\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" print(salary + bonus)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"add_bonus(\" /><text value=\"1900\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"37\" endIndex=\"42\" /><option startIndex=\"43\" endIndex=\"44\" /><option startIndex=\"45\" endIndex=\"48\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"2100\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>bonus</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>200</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You can only access or update a local variable inside the function that created it.</p><p>Update <code>bonus</code> so the code prints <code>2100</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"add_bonus\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(salary)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" bonus = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" bonus = \" /><text value=\"200\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" print(salary + bonus)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"add_bonus(\" /><text value=\"1900\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"37\" endIndex=\"42\" /><option startIndex=\"43\" endIndex=\"44\" /><option startIndex=\"45\" endIndex=\"48\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"salary\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"100\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"2100\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>bonus</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>200</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Error",
            "id": 86992,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>If we try to access or update the variable outside of the function block, like here with <code>bonus</code>, we'll get an error.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"add_bonus\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(salary)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" bonus = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" print(salary + bonus)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(bonus)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"add_bonus(\" /><text value=\"1900\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"71\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"NameError: name 'bonus' is not defined\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>bonus</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Local scope",
            "id": 87035,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When does a variable have a local scope?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">When we create it inside of a function's block</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Variables always have a local scope</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">When we create it inside of a function's block.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You create <code>title</code> outside all functions and <code>message</code> inside <code>greet()</code>. Which has local scope?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>message</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>title</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Both <code>title</code> and <code>message</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>message</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Local scope 2",
            "id": 87036,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does it mean for a variable to have a local scope?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">We can't access or update it outside of the function where it was created</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">We can access it from anywhere in the code</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">We can't access or update it outside of the function where it was created.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Accessing a local variable outside the function that created it causes an error.</p><p>You call a function that creates <code>discount = 5</code>, then try <code>print(discount)</code> outside it. What happens?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Python reports an error because <code>discount</code> is local to the function.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Python displays <code>5</code> because the function created the variable.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Python displays <code>None</code> because the variable is outside the function.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Python reports an error because <code>discount</code> is local to the function.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Error",
            "id": 87037,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What happens when we try to access a local scope variable outside of the function that created it?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">We get an error</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Nothing happens, we can access it</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">We get an error.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Trying to access a local variable outside the function that created it causes an error.</p><p>A function creates <code>total</code>. Which change lets the function display that value without a scope error?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Move <code>print(total)</code> inside the function's code block.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Call the function first, then use <code>print(total)</code> outside it.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Rename <code>total</code> only in the outside <code>print()</code> call.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Move <code>print(total)</code> inside the function's code block.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Local scope",
            "id": 87038,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create the variable <code>discount</code>, that has a local scope inside the <code>apply_discount</code> function.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"apply_discount\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(price)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  discount = \" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" price - discount\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"final_price = apply_discount(\" /><text value=\"50\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(final_price)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"29\" endIndex=\"37\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"30\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>discount</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Local scope 2",
            "id": 87039,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Update the variable <code>discount</code> to <code>10</code> within the local scope of <code>apply_discount</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"apply_discount\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(price)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  discount = \" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  discount = \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" price - discount\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"final_price = apply_discount(\" /><text value=\"50\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(final_price)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"45\" endIndex=\"58\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"40\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>discount = 10</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Error",
            "id": 87040,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Code a line to print the greeting message without accessing the variable <code>greeting</code> outside of its local scope of the <code>greet_user</code> function.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Amy&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"greet_user\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(name)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  greeting = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Hi&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;\" /><text value=\"{greeting}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{user}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Hi \" /><text value=\"{user}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"85\" endIndex=\"90\" /><option startIndex=\"90\" endIndex=\"91\" /><option startIndex=\"91\" endIndex=\"92\" /><option startIndex=\"92\" endIndex=\"104\" /><option startIndex=\"104\" endIndex=\"105\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Hi Amy!\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>print</code> followed by <code>(</code> and then <code>f</code>, <code>\"Hi {user}!\"</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The variable <code>greeting</code> is local to <code>greet_user</code>, so you cannot use it out here. Build a line that prints <code>Hi Amy!</code> on its own.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Amy&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"greet_user\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(name)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  greeting = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Hi&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;\" /><text value=\"{greeting}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{user}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Hi \" /><text value=\"{user}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"85\" endIndex=\"90\" /><option startIndex=\"90\" endIndex=\"91\" /><option startIndex=\"91\" endIndex=\"92\" /><option startIndex=\"92\" endIndex=\"104\" /><option startIndex=\"104\" endIndex=\"105\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;{greeting} {user}!&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;Hi {name}!&quot;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Hi Amy!\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>print</code>, followed by <code>(</code>, <code>f</code>, <code>\"Hi {user}!\"</code>, and finally <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": 9778,
        "title": "Global scope",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Global scope 1",
            "id": 86994,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Variables created outside of a function block have a <strong>global scope</strong>, like <code>shipping</code> here.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"shipping = \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"calculate_total\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(cart)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" print(cart + shipping)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"calculate_total(\" /><text value=\"54\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option startIndex=\"9\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"13\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"64\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>shipping</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>10</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A variable created outside a function has a <strong>global scope</strong>, so the function can read it. Create <code>shipping</code> as <code>10</code> to print <code>64</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"shipping = \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"calculate_total\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(cart)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" print(cart + shipping)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"calculate_total(\" /><text value=\"54\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option startIndex=\"9\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"13\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"cart\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"5\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"64\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>shipping</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>10</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Global access",
            "id": 86995,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>With a global scope, we can safely <strong>access</strong> the variable anywhere in the code, as we did with <code>shipping</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"shipping = \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"calculate_total\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(cart)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" print(cart + shipping)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"calculate_total(\" /><text value=\"54\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"64\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"64\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>shipping</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Global scope 2",
            "id": 86996,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>All variables have a global scope, except for those created inside functions, like player_1 here.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"single_player = \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" single_player:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" player_1 = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Mario&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Player 1: \" /><text value=\"{player_1}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"41\" endIndex=\"49\" /><option startIndex=\"50\" endIndex=\"51\" /><option startIndex=\"52\" endIndex=\"59\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Player 1: Mario\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>player_1</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>\"Mario\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>An <code>if</code> block is not a function, so <code>player_1</code> here keeps a global scope. Set it to <code>\"Mario\"</code> to print <code>Player 1: Mario</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"single_player = \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" single_player:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" player_1 = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Mario&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Player 1: \" /><text value=\"{player_1}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"41\" endIndex=\"49\" /><option startIndex=\"50\" endIndex=\"51\" /><option startIndex=\"52\" endIndex=\"59\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"single_player\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;Luigi&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Player 1: Mario\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>player_1</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>\"Mario\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Access after creating",
            "id": 86997,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Even with a global scope, it's important that we can only access variables after we create them, like here with <code>character</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"character = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Mario&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(character)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"36\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"if\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Mario\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>character = \"Mario\"</code>, followed by <code>print(character)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Even a global variable can only be used after it is created.</p><p>Store <code>\"Mario\"</code> in <code>character</code>, copy its value into <code>message</code>, then print <code>message</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"character\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"=\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"&quot;Mario&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"message\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"=\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"character\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"message\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"39\" /><option startIndex=\"40\" endIndex=\"54\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"message = &quot;character&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"print(&quot;message&quot;)\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Mario\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>character = \"Mario\"</code>, followed by <code>message = character</code>, and finally <code>print(message)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Global scope 1",
            "id": 87041,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which variables have a global scope?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Variables created outside of a function's block</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">All variables</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Variables created outside of a function's block.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Variables created outside a function's block have global scope.</p><p>The line <code>theme = \"dark\"</code> appears before any function definition. Which scope does <code>theme</code> have?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Global scope</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Local scope</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Parameter scope</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick Global scope.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Global access",
            "id": 87042,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>From where can we access a variable with a global scope?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">From anywhere in the code</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Only inside functions</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">From anywhere in the code.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You can access a global variable from anywhere in the code.</p><p>You set global <code>tax = 5</code>. A function returns <code>price + tax</code>. What does it return when passed <code>10</code> for <code>price</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>15</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>10</code>, because the function ignores outside variables.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">An error, because <code>tax</code> was created outside the function.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>15</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Questions: Global scope 2",
            "id": 87043,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What kind of scope do variables created inside conditionals and loops have?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Local</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Global, because they're not created inside functions</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick Local.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Conditionals and loops do not create a new local scope in Python.</p><p>A top-level <code>while</code> loop creates <code>attempts = 1</code> in its block. Which scope does <code>attempts</code> have?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Global scope, because the loop does not create a new scope</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Local scope, because the assignment is indented inside the loop</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">No scope until the loop finishes</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Global scope, because the loop does not create a new scope.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Access after creating",
            "id": 87044,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When can we first access a variable, regardless of scope?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Only after we create it</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Before or after creating it</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Only after we create it.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Regardless of scope, we can first access a variable only after we create it.</p><p>Which order displays <code>10</code> without an error?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">First <code>score = 10</code>, then <code>print(score)</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">First <code>print(score)</code>, then <code>score = 10</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Only <code>print(score)</code>, because printing creates the variable</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">First <code>score = 10</code>, then <code>print(score)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Global scope 1",
            "id": 87045,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create <code>rent</code> outside of the function, so that it has a global scope.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"rent = \" /><text value=\"1000\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"calculate_spendings\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(groceries)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Total: \" /><text value=\"{rent + groceries}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Rent: \" /><text value=\"{rent}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"calculate_spendings(\" /><text value=\"300\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"4\" /><option startIndex=\"5\" endIndex=\"6\" /><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"11\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Rent: 1000\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Total: 1300\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>rent</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>1000</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create <code>rent</code> outside the function so the function and outer print can read it. Set it to <code>1000</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"rent = \" /><text value=\"1000\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"calculate_spendings\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(groceries)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Total: \" /><text value=\"{rent + groceries}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Rent: \" /><text value=\"{rent}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"calculate_spendings(\" /><text value=\"300\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"4\" /><option startIndex=\"5\" endIndex=\"6\" /><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"11\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"groceries\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"100\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Rent: 1000\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Total: 1300\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>rent</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>1000</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Global access",
            "id": 87046,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Access the global variable <code>rent</code> inside the function.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"rent = \" /><text value=\"1000\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"calculate_spendings\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(groceries)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Total \" /><text value=\"{rent + groceries}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Rent \" /><text value=\"{rent}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"calculate_spendings(\" /><text value=\"300\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"70\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Rent 1000\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Total 1300\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>rent</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Global scope 2",
            "id": 87047,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create the global variable <code>discount</code>, then display it outside of the loop.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"price = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"discount = \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i \" /><text value=\"in\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" range(\" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"):\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  price = price - discount\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Discount: \" /><text value=\"{discount}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Price: \" /><text value=\"{price}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"25\" /><option startIndex=\"73\" endIndex=\"103\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Discount: 10\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Price: 80\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>discount = 10</code>, followed by <code>print(f\"Discount: {discount}\")</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A <code>for</code> loop is not a function, so <code>discount</code> stays global.</p><p>Create it as <code>10</code>, then display it after the loop to print <code>Discount: 10</code> and <code>Price: 80</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"price = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"discount = \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i \" /><text value=\"in\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" range(\" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"):\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  price = price - discount\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Discount: \" /><text value=\"{discount}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Price: \" /><text value=\"{price}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"25\" /><option startIndex=\"73\" endIndex=\"103\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"discount = 20\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"print(discount)\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Discount: 10\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Price: 80\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>discount = 10</code>, followed by <code>print(f\"Discount: {discount}\")</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
